Chapter: EqNullaryEnumOk
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A nullary-only enum carries a sound tag-based Eq/Ord even without
 deriving (the tag is the value), so == on it still type-checks with
 no cdx-no-class-instance and dispatches to the built-in tag compare.

Section: Types

  Dir = | North | South | East | West

Section: Opening

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (if North == North then "eq" else "ne")
    print-line-uni (if North == South then "eq" else "ne")
  end

